// frontseat.plugin.v1alpha1: what a plugin is asked and what it answers.
//
// A plugin is a wasm module. It reads the repository only through the host
// (host.proto), so the host sees every read; the same reads and the same
// request give the same answer. It runs nothing: it declares actions, and
// the host runs them on the grid.
//
// This file, host.proto, release.proto, abi.proto and the ABI document
// beside them (ABI.md) are the whole contract. A plugin in any language
// that compiles to wasm needs nothing else, and an SDK is a convenience
// over the types generated from these files.
//
// A plugin says what it is (Describe), and serves what of the rest it is
// for: it finds projects and declares their actions (Analyze), tells its
// tool what they were handed (Arrange) and says what a check of its found
// (Report); it finds catalog entities (Analyze) and says what their files
// should say (Reconcile); it says how a service is started for a test
// (Service); it is a release strategy (Branch, Version). Every plugin
// serves Describe, Analyze and Arrange. A method it does not serve it
// answers UNIMPLEMENTED, for the method's own reason: REPORT_NOT_SERVED,
// RECONCILE_NOT_SERVED and SERVICE_NOT_SERVED, the method's name in
// capitals; BRANCHING_STRATEGY_NOT_SERVED and
// VERSIONING_STRATEGY_NOT_SERVED, the kind of strategy, which is also
// the answer for a strategy, or a service, it does not claim. A name here
